Those "ports" are "official", to the extent that you're extremely likely to get 
support from the devteam if you're having trouble getting things configured & 
compiled on those platforms. In fact, I would guess that for any given member 
of that list, devteam, or someone they know, is very likely to have a 
corresponding physical machine available (perhaps only temporarily) for 
testing. Those bugs get fixed. Binaries maybe just don't happen to be 
available in a some centralized repository, but that doesn't necessarily mean 
we shouldn't call it an "official" port. See below.

